// Mandatory braces, the emptiest case: `if (x);` binds the branch to NOTHING and the statement after it
// runs unconditionally. It parses to a null body (empty_statement has an empty action), so the check must
// reject a null body rather than skip it — this is the purest form of the bug the rule exists to kill.
fn int32 main() {
    int32 x = 1;
    if (x > 0);
    return 0;
}
